WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:04.711
What if a roofing website helped homeowners explore the decision before the first conversation?

2
00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:08.336
This is Velar, a concept built by Wallace Shift.

3
00:00:08.971 --> 00:00:13.914
An architectural opening and material collection lead into a roof design studio.

4
00:00:14.555 --> 00:00:18.416
Upload a photograph, then choose a material and finish.

5
00:00:18.676 --> 00:00:23.058
The photo is prepared locally, with consent required before sending it for generation.

6
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.632
We are using prepared sample studies here.

7
00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:30.149
Compare the original with slate, then explore the same home in metal.

8
00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:35.538
Enter measured roof area and complexity to explore an illustrative planning range.

9
00:00:35.798 --> 00:00:38.250
The photograph itself does not measure the roof.

10
00:00:38.888 --> 00:00:43.284
Those choices carry into a project brief, keeping the conversation connected.

11
00:00:43.544 --> 00:00:46.923
This demo prepares the brief locally; nothing is sent.

12
00:00:47.555 --> 00:00:54.360
A separate sample project room shows how approvals, site updates and documents could be presented after the sale.

13
00:00:54.972 --> 00:00:57.673
From first impression to a more informed conversation.

14
00:00:57.933 --> 00:01:00.903
A tailored roofing experience, by Wallace Shift.
